# Project Log Mandate

After completing a **significant unit of work** (stage slice, band, fix arc, or multi-file feature), **always append** an entry to [`docs/project_log.md`](docs/project_log.md).

Do **not** skip this because the user did not ask. Do **not** edit the plan file instead of the log. Do **not** overwrite prior entries — **append only**.

## When to write

- A roadmap stage / sub-stage / band checklist item is finished (or a coherent fix arc closes)
- A multi-file feature lands (Edge Functions, migrations, Flutter stack, etc.)
- A production/local incident is diagnosed and fixed (e.g. sync LAN/JWT/grants)
- Before ending a long Agent turn that shipped substantive work

Skip only for trivial one-liners (typo, comment) with no behavior or docs impact.

## Entry format (append at end of file)

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — <Stage / Band / Title>

### Context
What was requested and why (1–3 sentences).

### Done
- Concrete deliverables with **file paths** and roadmap refs (§x.y)

### Architecture / decisions
Locked choices, invariants preserved, explicit non-goals

### Ops / verification
Commands run, test counts, migrate/deploy notes, known follow-ups

### Status
Roadmap checkboxes updated? Blockers for the next band?
```

## Quality bar

- Accurate and **organized** — usable by the owner, the next developer, and future AI sessions
- Prefer paths + § references over vague “wired sync”
- Call out **remaining gaps** honestly (stubs, deferred FCM, unchecked invite acceptance, etc.)
- If `docs/project_log.md` is missing, create it with a one-line title `# Daftar — Project Log` then append
